# vpl · what every answer from this app carries
#
# The policy is the same in all eight, and `serve.py` sends it too, so what is
# tested locally is what is deployed. Why each allowance is there (C8 in
# docs/security.md — "every XSS would be the model key", because the key lives in
# localStorage):
#
#   script-src        jsdelivr: marked, DOMPurify, pdf.js, and supabase-js's UMD
#                     build. 'wasm-unsafe-eval' is pdf.js's decoder, not eval().
#   style-src         'unsafe-inline' is for the five `style="--x:9%"` attributes
#                     in vi's funnel drawing; without it the drawing collapses.
#   font-src          vi's three Google faces.
#   connect-src       Supabase REST/auth/storage, the suite's own door, jsdelivr.
#   worker-src        the pdf.js worker, a module loaded from the CDN.
#   frame/object/base the app never frames, never embeds, never rebases a url.
#
# A change here that an app needs must also land in serve.py, or the local suite
# tests a page that does not exist in production.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://api.terg.hr https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; worker-src 'self' blob: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
